# ============================================================
# THE COMING SOON FLAG. One value, two readers, one edit to reverse.
# ============================================================
#
# This page ships at launch as a placeholder, so it must not be indexed and
# must not appear in sitemap.xml. Both come from this one boolean: base.njk
# reads it through `pageNoindex` to emit the robots meta tag, and sitemap.njk
# filters on the same computed value. Two independent switches is how a page
# ends up listed in a sitemap while still carrying noindex, which is a
# contradiction handed to a crawler.
#
# NOT A robots.txt Disallow, deliberately. Blocking /library/ there would stop
# a crawler ever fetching the page, and a directive that is never fetched is
# never read. Meta noindex needs the page crawlable. src/robots.njk argues the
# same case at length for the preview host and it transfers exactly.
#
# THE FLIP CHECKLIST, when articles start publishing here:
#
#   1. Set this to false.
#   2. Replace the placeholder copy below, and the placeholder hero.
#   3. Confirm /library/ is linked. It already is, src/_data/nav.js footer.
#   4. Repoint /blog in src/_redirects from /yelp/ to /library/. It is a 302
#      today precisely so this is cheap.
#   5. Submit https://www.circulationstudio.com/library/ in Search Console.
#
# The same checklist is in .claude/CLAUDE.md, because a checklist that lives
# only in the file being changed is one nobody reads before deciding to change
# it. The build also refuses to let this go stale: a real article in
# src/library/ while this is still true fails the build. See eleventy.config.js,
# the eleventy.after hook.
comingSoon: true

# THE HERO IMAGE IS A PLACEHOLDER. Two other candidates are in play and the
# choice is not made, so swapping it is these four lines and nothing else.
#
# ONE FILENAME, DELIBERATELY. `preloadImage` is what base.njk preloads AND
# what the <img> takes as its src, so the two cannot drift apart. A preload
# pointing at a file the page does not use is a wasted download and a missed
# LCP, and it is the failure that happens when a swap edits one and not the
# other.
#
# The dimensions are the file's true intrinsic size and MUST be re-read from
# the replacement. The frame sets no height, so this pair is what reserves the
# space, and a stale pair reintroduces layout shift on the page's LCP element.
preloadImage: cs-img-leaves-landscape.webp
heroWidth: 1400
heroHeight: 784
heroAlt: Leaves ranged in a row, one subject studied specimen by specimen
---
