      NOT THE NETWORK PATTERN, and not by omission. That hero puts type on the
      photograph because the photograph reserves a column of paper beside the
      subject. This one reserves its paper ABOVE a row of leaves, so the same
      move would drop the type onto the leaves themselves.

      It also would not survive the swap. Two other candidates are in play, and
      any layout that positions type against a particular part of the frame has
      to be re-measured when the frame changes. The rule this follows is that
      nothing here knows what is in the picture: full measure, natural ratio,
